{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/3","id":4134027343,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTVpH8872aEBP","html_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/3","diff_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/3.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/3.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/issues/3","number":3,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"bog-bench — a benchmark harness for agent tooling, on fold","user":{"login":"mrojas54","id":49874076,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODc0MDc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49874076?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54","html_url":"https://github.com/mrojas54","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrojas54/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Hackathon submission\n\n### category\n\n- [ ] agent support\n- [x] performance\n- [ ] novel interface / gaming\n\n### team\n\n- **project name:** bog-bench\n- **team / author name(s):** mrojas54 (built with Claude Code as a pair)\n- **contact (optional):** via this PR\n\n### what you built\n\n**Fold one newly completed session into persistent aggregate views without\nrescanning prior sessions; three local five-trial measurements kept append cost\nin the same tens-of-milliseconds range across 51–801 sessions.**\n\n![bog-bench application and fold architecture, including exact retraction, isolated windows, and local benchmark measurements](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrojas54/bogkit/bog-bench/examples/bog-bench/assets/bog-bench-overview.webp)\n\nbog-bench turns Claude Code tool calls into persistent `fold` materialized\nviews: corpus totals, per-tool rows, explicit-error and unknown-outcome counts,\nper-session rows, and an exact counted bag of the ingested calls.\n\nThe exact-call bag fixes the two shipping blockers identified in final review:\n\n- `demo` now owns a process-unique scratch database, while no-argument\n  invocation prints help without opening persistent state;\n- transcript identity is the canonical path, growing files reconcile by\n  atomically replacing their prior stored snapshot, and `retract` removes only\n  that stored snapshot instead of reparsing possibly changed contents.\n\nOrdinary ingest updates persistent aggregate views from deltas without\nrescanning prior sessions. Reconciliation touches the selected session\nsnapshot. `window` is a separate full event-time replay into a scratch stream.\n\nUnmatched calls are `Unknown`, not successful. `ERROR%` is explicit errors over\nknown outcomes, malformed/unmatched input emits parser diagnostics, and `CHARS`\nmeans normalized joined-result characters—not raw payload bytes or total model\ncontext cost.\n\nThe corrected six-branch architecture and persistence boundaries are in\n[`examples/bog-bench/README.md`](examples/bog-bench/README.md#materialized-views).\n\n### how to run\n\n```bash\ncargo run -p bog-bench --             # help; no state mutation\ncargo run -p bog-bench -- demo        # isolated fixtures\ncargo test -p bog-bench               # 19 debug-build tests\ncargo test --release -p bog-bench     # 18 release-build tests\n```\n\n`demo` ingests one fixture session, appends another, then retracts it:\n\n```text\n== appended session-b — views moved, nothing rescanned ==\n9 tool calls · 3 explicit errors among 9 known outcomes · 0 unknown outcomes\n\n  TOOL                        CALLS  ERROR    UNK  ERROR%       CHARS     ~TOK\n  Read                            3      0      0      0%       67600    16900\n  Bash                            4      3      0     75%        6640     1660\n  Grep                            1      0      0      0%        3300      825\n  Edit                            1      0      0      0%         180       45\n\n== retracted session-b — every counter rolled back ==\n5 tool calls · 1 explicit error among 5 known outcomes · 0 unknown outcomes\n```\n\n`Grep` disappears because it existed only in the stored snapshot that was\nretracted. `recent`, `show`, `ingest`, `retract`, `bench`, `window`, and `reset`\nread the local corpus under `~/.claude/projects`.\n\n### benchmark evidence\n\n```bash\ncargo run -p bog-bench -- bench 800 5\n```\n\nEach trial compares total calls, explicit-error and unknown counts, every\nper-tool row, every per-session row, and the exact-call bag before reporting\ntimings. A mismatch exits non-zero.\n\nLocal environment: `macos/aarch64`, debug profile, 8 logical CPUs, five trials\nper corpus size.\n\n| corpus | arriving calls | incremental total median (min–max, σ) | full rescan total median (min–max, σ) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 51 sessions | 290 | 32.5 ms (29.0–37.2, 2.7) | 680.9 ms (601.4–717.2, 42.0) |\n| 201 sessions | 291 | 40.7 ms (35.8–70.9, 14.2) | 749.1 ms (704.9–1,050.0, 133.2) |\n| 801 sessions | 292 | 48.6 ms (38.4–50.8, 4.6) | 1,052.2 ms (908.6–1,154.0, 82.4) |\n\nThe selected private corpus was live, so the newest transcript grew slightly\nbetween commands. These runs show incremental work remaining in the same\ntens-of-milliseconds range while full replay grew across this local range. They\nare measurements, not a durable complexity guarantee; other machines, stores,\ncorpora, profiles, and workloads need their own repeated trials.\n\nThe comparison arm is a full-rescan batch design; incremental or cached systems\ncan also avoid rescans but must supply their own persistence and retraction\nsemantics. There is no cross-engine throughput comparison.\n\nThis output could support a future CI policy. The current CLI reports metrics\nbut does not define a baseline, threshold, or pass/fail gate.\n\n### verification\n\nFull local code gate at head `4682c1f`:\n\n- scoped `rustfmt --check`;\n- `cargo clippy -p bog-bench --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`;\n- 19 debug and 18 release `bog-bench` tests;\n- `cargo test --workspace` and `cargo test --workspace --release`, including\n  doctests;\n- a concurrent two-process regression proving scratch test stores no longer\n  collide.\n\nThe docs-only visual head `950807d` separately passed `git diff --check`,\na 1672×941 WebP inspection, and `cargo test -p bog-bench` (19 tests).\n\nRepository CI now runs the workspace test suite in both debug and release\nprofiles.\n\nSeventeen tests are deterministic and fixture-based. Two local-corpus smoke\nchecks return early when no corpus is present.\n\nIn one private 114-session corpus, the parser recorded 2,668 tool calls, 100\ncarrying explicit error flags. One browser-automation tool had 5 flagged errors\nacross 10 calls and averaged approximately 4,200 normalized result characters\nper call. These observations are not independently reproducible from this PR.\n\n### checklist\n\n- [x] i forked bog-kit and built my project in this fork\n- [x] my project is runnable from this pr (crate name and run command above)\n- [x] i selected exactly one category\n- [x] this pr is my official hackathon submission acknowledgment\n","created_at":"2026-07-25T21:40:49Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T13:53:16Z","closed_at":"2026-08-16T13:53:16Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"915425356005a9a53eac79e67c0d2ff2a17e825b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/3/commits","review_